1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,609
Last time the ruin could talk.

2
00:00:03,059 --> 00:00:05,233
Today it has a story.

3
00:00:05,683 --> 00:00:11,335
Four steps, one after another, each in a different part of the ruin.

4
00:00:11,785 --> 00:00:17,437
The crew is paid for each, and the last one ends the game.

5
00:00:17,887 --> 00:00:21,365
I did not open the script file once.

6
00:00:22,565 --> 00:00:29,957
There is a shipped campaign called Storm's Beacon, and it is made of ruins like this one.

7
00:00:30,407 --> 00:00:35,624
Each ruin is one episode, and every episode is the same chain.

8
00:00:36,074 --> 00:00:40,422
The approach: the crew comes up to the way in.

9
00:00:40,872 --> 00:00:47,828
A call: somebody who knows the place tells them something. A room. A call. A room.

10
00:00:48,278 --> 00:00:54,365
And at the end, the piece: they take away what the ruin was hiding.

11
00:00:54,815 --> 00:00:58,728
You can already write every link in that chain.

12
00:00:59,178 --> 00:01:04,396
A step that finishes when the ship gets somewhere is Class 1.

13
00:01:04,846 --> 00:01:09,193
A call when the ship gets somewhere is last lecture.

14
00:01:09,643 --> 00:01:14,426
A step that waits for a word is Class 1 again.

15
00:01:14,876 --> 00:01:19,659
Here is what is new today: where the word comes from.

16
00:01:20,109 --> 00:01:25,761
Nobody can leave the ship until next lecture, so today Comms says it.

17
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:29,135
The story needs a heading.

18
00:01:29,585 --> 00:01:35,237
An arc: three hashes, and the word Arc alone on the first line.

19
00:01:35,687 --> 00:01:37,426
It starts at once.

20
00:01:37,876 --> 00:01:40,050
It fails after twenty minutes.

21
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:47,022
A Win sentence for when it is finished, a Lose sentence for when it fails.

22
00:01:47,472 --> 00:01:50,080
All of that is Class 1.

23
00:01:50,530 --> 00:01:57,052
Nobody warns the crew about the clock, so I say twenty minutes in the description.

24
00:01:58,252 --> 00:01:59,557
The first step.

25
00:02:00,007 --> 00:02:03,485
Four hashes, so it belongs to the arc.

26
00:02:03,935 --> 00:02:07,413
And this line: Done when: reach entrance 1000.

27
00:02:07,863 --> 00:02:13,515
Last time I wrote Starts when: reach altar 600, to start a beat.

28
00:02:13,965 --> 00:02:20,487
This is the same sentence in a Done when line, so it finishes a step.

29
00:02:20,937 --> 00:02:27,893
The rules have not changed. entrance is a role: the word on the place's Roles line.

30
00:02:28,343 --> 00:02:30,517
This place's key is way_in.

31
00:02:30,967 --> 00:02:35,750
The key does not work here, and lint will tell you.

32
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:38,374
A thousand is how close.

33
00:02:38,824 --> 00:02:40,998
And always write the number.

34
00:02:41,448 --> 00:02:49,709
Without it the game uses five thousand, and the step is finished before the crew has seen the ruin.

35
00:02:50,159 --> 00:02:59,724
One more thing for numbers inside a ruin: the game looks every two seconds, so do not go below about three hundred.

36
00:03:00,924 --> 00:03:02,228
Two more steps.

37
00:03:02,678 --> 00:03:06,591
Both say Starts when: revealed, so they are asleep.

38
00:03:07,041 --> 00:03:09,650
The way in reveals the first.

39
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:12,274
The first reveals the second.

40
00:03:12,724 --> 00:03:17,507
The full address every time: the arc, a slash, the step.

41
00:03:17,957 --> 00:03:22,304
Now look. reach altar 600 is in my file twice.

42
00:03:22,754 --> 00:03:27,972
On the beat, in a Starts when line, it starts the call.

43
00:03:28,422 --> 00:03:33,639
On the step, in a Done when line, it finishes the step.

44
00:03:34,089 --> 00:03:41,915
They happen together: the ship comes into the Vault, the step is done and Rook is on Comms.

45
00:03:42,365 --> 00:03:48,017
The second step sends the ship to the Niche, the place I hid.

46
00:03:48,467 --> 00:03:54,989
The crew can find it because Rook tells them, or because they go and look.

47
00:03:55,439 --> 00:04:01,091
So if Comms shuts the recording off, the story can still be finished.

48
00:04:02,291 --> 00:04:04,900
The last step is the piece.

49
00:04:05,350 --> 00:04:07,089
Somebody takes the thing.

50
00:04:07,539 --> 00:04:13,191
Nobody can leave the ship today, so this is a decision Comms makes.

51
00:04:13,641 --> 00:04:16,685
The step says Done when: signal hollow_taken.

52
00:04:17,135 --> 00:04:21,048
It waits for a word. hollow_taken is my word.

53
00:04:21,498 --> 00:04:27,150
And Action: the moment the step starts, Rook calls with a second recording.

54
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:30,643
Now the scene. Two takes. Two answers.

55
00:04:31,093 --> 00:04:35,876
One asks what it is, and leads to a second scene.

56
00:04:36,326 --> 00:04:41,109
One says take it aboard, and after the semicolon: signal hollow_taken.

57
00:04:41,559 --> 00:04:43,298
That sends the word.

58
00:04:43,748 --> 00:04:50,704
The step hears it, pays, and it was the last step, so the game is won.

59
00:04:51,154 --> 00:04:54,633
Look at the ways out of this conversation.

60
00:04:55,083 --> 00:04:58,561
There are two, and both send the word.

61
00:04:59,011 --> 00:05:00,750
That is on purpose.

62
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:12,070
If I add an answer that just hangs up, a crew that picks it has spent the call, and the step can never be finished.

63
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:17,302
The crew's way of saying not now is the Back button.

64
00:05:17,752 --> 00:05:22,970
Why a word, and not completes, the way Class 2 did it?

65
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:27,767
Because the step does not care who says the word.

66
00:05:28,217 --> 00:05:37,783
Next lecture a crew member can go and take the bowl by hand, and this step will not change by one letter.

67
00:05:38,983 --> 00:05:43,330
Last time I put a Scan line on the Altar.

68
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:46,824
That is for a person standing there.

69
00:05:47,274 --> 00:05:51,622
The Science console on the ship does not show it.

70
00:05:52,072 --> 00:05:55,985
Science reads scan records, the ones from Class 1.

71
00:05:56,435 --> 00:06:02,522
A place wears a role, and a role is all a scan record needs.

72
00:06:02,972 --> 00:06:06,450
Scan of, the role, a tab, a reading.

73
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:09,943
One on the place for a person.

74
00:06:10,393 --> 00:06:13,002
One in Scans for the ship.

75
00:06:14,202 --> 00:06:15,202
Lint. Clean.

76
00:06:15,652 --> 00:06:19,565
Now I use the key where the role goes.

77
00:06:20,015 --> 00:06:23,928
Nothing in this mission wears a role called way_in.

78
00:06:24,378 --> 00:06:27,422
Good: that step would never have finished.

79
00:06:27,872 --> 00:06:29,176
Put it back.

80
00:06:29,626 --> 00:06:33,104
Now I drop the arc from a reveal.

81
00:06:33,554 --> 00:06:39,641
It tells me the step is survey/first to the game, and to write that.

82
00:06:40,091 --> 00:06:41,396
Put it back.

83
00:06:41,846 --> 00:06:46,628
Now I take these two lines off the last step. Clean.

84
00:06:47,078 --> 00:06:48,817
And this one matters.

85
00:06:49,267 --> 00:06:53,180
The other three steps still say they are required.

86
00:06:53,630 --> 00:07:04,500
So the game decides the arc is finished when those three are, and the crew wins at the niche with the last call still ringing.

87
00:07:04,950 --> 00:07:06,689
Lint cannot see that.

88
00:07:07,139 --> 00:07:13,226
Read your steps: all of them have the two lines, or none of them.

89
00:07:14,426 --> 00:07:16,600
One step in the list.

90
00:07:17,050 --> 00:07:18,789
Fly to the door.

91
00:07:19,239 --> 00:07:22,717
Done, and paid, and here is the next.

92
00:07:23,167 --> 00:07:27,080
In through the Mouth, the Nave, up the tunnel.

93
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:30,139
Done again, and Rook is calling.

94
00:07:30,589 --> 00:07:34,067
Science: the Altar, and there is my reading.

95
00:07:34,517 --> 00:07:36,257
Comms: play the rest.

96
00:07:36,707 --> 00:07:38,011
Mark the Gallery.

97
00:07:38,461 --> 00:07:44,548
Back across the Nave, into the built room, to the far end. Third step.

98
00:07:44,998 --> 00:07:46,302
A second recording.

99
00:07:46,752 --> 00:07:48,057
Take it aboard.

100
00:07:48,507 --> 00:07:50,680
And that is the game.

101
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:54,489
Give the Altar a second tab.

102
00:07:54,939 --> 00:07:58,852
Add a fifth step that carries the bowl home.

103
00:07:59,302 --> 00:08:03,215
Give the crew a way to lose on purpose.

104
00:08:03,665 --> 00:08:09,752
Then break one line where lint can see it and one where it cannot.

105
00:08:10,202 --> 00:08:12,811
Next time, the crew goes outside.
